      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Crunch compression also hides how much VRAM an avatar takes up when uncompressed to the GPU. \nThe AvatarEvaluator is great for checking this, and I believe we should have a VRAM use limit for green/medium avys. \nhttps://github.com/Thryrallo/VRCAvatarTools/releases/tag/ava_eval_0.5",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-09-06T06:44:31.725Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is already in the log but it can be added to the SDK Upload\nUsers do not understand how VRAM intensive their avatars are, with alot of avatars being over 70mb\nThis is becoming a more and more of a problem, the avatar size is getting exponentially too large, people are just putting 4k textures and not knowing how much vram it eats. The avatar Ranking system doesn't count this towards stats, an avatar could be Very Good performance but the model is 200+ mb\nAnd the new fallback system doesn't even check for file size, you can upload a 400+mb fallback and eat all the VRAM and you can't disable it",
